    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265-a6">

                <pb facs="0488" n="388" xml:id="pg388"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State and of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1880-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 26, 1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The chief clerk in charge of the department of public works writes as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Ignacio Garfias</hi>: I have the honor to
                    transmit it to you for your information, and of result of your communication of
                    the 8th (?), of 1879, staging that in view of the scientific report of Engineer
                    Garfias, inclosed in this communication, and of the one sent by the consul of
                    Mexico in Rio Grande City, which I had the honor to inclose in my dispatch of
                    the 7th of February last, that the islands of Sabinito and Morteritos, situated
                    near Roma, Tex., belong entirely to the territory of the Republic.”</p>
                <closer><signed>RUELLAS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To the <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State and of the Department of
                            the Treasury</hi>.</p>
                    <p>A true copy.</p>
                    <closer><signed>CAYETANO ROMERO,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary.</hi></signed>
                        <lb/>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1884-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 12,
                            1884</date>.</dateline>
                    </closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
